The fresh false-result mutation behaved exactly as required: it parsed and compiled in dry-run mode (exit 0), then `kprove` exited 1 with a reachable stuck implication showing `decodeSpec(CS)` cannot satisfy `encodeSpec(CS)`. That confirms the entry theorem genuinely constrains the returned value. I’m consolidating the seven-stage findings and trust ledger into `REVIEW.md`; the remaining judgment is about the deliberately narrow generated-Python model, not proof closure.
